the package and what's needed to be
known as soon as one goes inside it. And

00:01:51.520 --> 00:01:58.240
then you know making sure that it that
it is at the right level of detail. Not

00:01:55.759 --> 00:02:02.960
so much detail that it consumes context
but enough so that the right core

00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:07.360
functions are called in that package.
That is the trick and that takes time

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:10.720
and effort. You can get of course claw
code to write this for you. But then you

00:02:09.039 --> 00:02:15.360
need to eyeball it and make sure you're
satisfied with it. Do a couple of rounds

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:21.920
of reviews. Invest time in your
agents.md. It will pay dividends. And

00:02:18.640 --> 00:02:27.200
also project documentation for agents is
what it's all about. If you if you have

00:02:24.239 --> 00:02:31.760
a document that you tag with the at sign
then that gets inserted into in it

00:02:29.599 --> 00:02:35.920
entirety into that that that outer
document which is not normally what you

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:40.480
want. Better is to describe what a
document does and then and then put a

00:02:37.760 --> 00:02:44.959
link to it because then claude code or
the other coding agent can decide does

00:02:42.800 --> 00:02:50.160
it need to know about this document and
if so it will read it. So structuring

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:54.319
your documents to to be summarizing and
then to be pointing to more detailed

00:02:51.840 --> 00:03:00.239
documents so that an agent can navigate
properly that is a a key to success with

00:02:57.680 --> 00:03:04.560
big code bases and taking time to get
that documentation and making sure that

00:03:02.159 --> 00:03:08.800
it's up to date as changes happen.
Always make sure there's a step when

00:03:06.480 --> 00:03:15.760
